<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">14 events that happened on 2 January, from 533 to 2004.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/533">533 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,493 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mercurius becomes Pope John II, the first pope to change his name</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Roman priest Mercurius, reluctant to reign under the name of a pagan god, took the name John II on his consecration. Adopting a papal name later became the settled custom of the Church.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1492">1492 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Granada surrenders to Ferdinand and Isabella</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> Muhammad XII handed the keys of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> to the Catholic Monarchs, ending the last Muslim state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> after nearly eight centuries. Months later the same monarchs sponsored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a>'s first voyage.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maria-theresa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Maria Theresa abolishes judicial torture in Austria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Persuaded by reformers such as Joseph von Sonnenfels, Empress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> ended the use of torture in criminal proceedings in her Austrian and Bohemian lands. It was a landmark of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a> legal reform.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1777">1777 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Washington repulses Cornwallis at Assunpink Creek</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Second Battle of Trenton, Washington's army held the bridge over Assunpink <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> against repeated British attacks. That night the Americans slipped away to strike Princeton the next morning.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1788">1788 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">238 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Georgia ratifies the US Constitution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>'s convention voted unanimously to ratify the new federal Constitution, making it the fourth state to do so. A frontier state facing conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>, Georgia valued the protection of a stronger union.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1818">1818 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">208 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Institution of Civil Engineers founded in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Three young engineers met at a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> house to found the Institution of Civil Engineers. Under Thomas Telford, its president from 1820, it became the model for professional engineering bodies worldwide.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1863">1863 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Union holds the field at the Battle of Stones River</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A failed Confederate assault on the final day of fighting near Murfreesboro, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>, led Braxton Bragg to withdraw. The costly Union success lifted Northern morale after the defeat at Fredericksburg.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1900">1900 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">126 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Hay promotes the Open Door Policy towards China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">US Secretary of State John Hay pressed the great powers to grant equal trading rights in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and respect its territorial integrity. The Open Door became a cornerstone of American policy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1920">1920 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Palmer Raids sweep up thousands of suspected radicals</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Federal agents directed by Attorney General A. Mitchell Palmer arrested thousands of suspected communists and anarchists in cities across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. The raids marked the height of the first Red Scare.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1942">1942 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japanese forces occupy Manila</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a>, declared an open city after American and Filipino forces withdrew to Bataan. The Philippine capital remained under Japanese occupation until its devastating liberation in 1945.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1954">1954 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">72 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">India institutes the Bharat Ratna, its highest civilian award</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajendra-prasad">Rajendra Prasad</a> established the Bharat Ratna to honour exceptional national service. The first recipients were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/c-rajagopalachari">C. Rajagopalachari</a>, Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan and the physicist C. V. Raman.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1959">1959 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">67 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Union launches Luna 1 towards the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Luna 1 lifted off from Baikonur and became the first spacecraft to reach escape velocity. It missed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a> but passed close by and entered orbit around the Sun, the first human-made object to do so.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Viet Cong defeat a larger South Vietnamese force at Ap Bac</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Communist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrillas</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-delta">Mekong Delta</a> beat off a South Vietnamese attack backed by American helicopters and advisers. The battle exposed weaknesses in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh-city">Saigon</a> army and US optimism about the war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2004">2004 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">22 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">NASA's Stardust probe flies through the tail of comet Wild 2</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Stardust passed within about 240 km of comet Wild 2's nucleus, collecting dust in blocks of aerogel. The samples, returned to Earth in 2006, were the first material ever brought back from a comet.</p></div></li></ol>
